{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3052","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3052","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3052\",\"parent_revision\":\"0c58940fc717c69a0b93c7d1bea1d3c763db667024bb56491543baa18934cfcb\",\"root_revision\":\"0c58940fc717c69a0b93c7d1bea1d3c763db667024bb56491543baa18934cfcb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `backlog_view` parameter table in `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` omits several parameters that exist in the server signature (`backlog_core/server.py`): `summary`, `show`, `since`, `section`, and `sections`.\\n\\nThe most consequential omission is `summary`. It defaults to `True` and returns a compact routing manifest rather than full item content \u2014 and the skill's documented \\\"Returns\\\" contract does not describe that shape at all. An agent reading only the skill doc does not know what the default call actually hands back. The plugin's own `AGENTS.md` example passes `{\\\"selector\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"summary\\\": false}` explicitly, which implies the default is understood internally but never written down where agents read it.\\n\\nThis is the same class of defect as the progressive-disclosure gap addressed in PR #3051 (`map`/`navigate`/`head`/`skip_tokens` were implemented and tested but absent from agent-facing documentation, and consequently used by no consuming agent). That PR was deliberately scoped to the disclosure parameters; this item covers the remaining drift.\\n\\n### Root pattern worth addressing\\n\\nBoth gaps share one cause: the MCP tool signature in `server.py` is the source of truth for parameters, and the skill documentation is maintained by hand against it with nothing enforcing agreement. Parameters can be added to the server indefinitely without the agent-facing doc changing, and no test or lint gate detects the divergence.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Every parameter in the `backlog_view` server signature appears in the skill's parameter table with its type, default, and purpose\\n- [ ] The default return shape (`summary=True`, the compact routing manifest) is documented in the Returns contract, distinctly from the `summary=False` full-content shape\\n- [ ] A mechanism is proposed (not necessarily implemented in this item) that detects future divergence between an MCP tool signature and its agent-facing documentation\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs an **agent calling `backlog_view`**, I want **the skill documentation to describe every implemented parameter and the actual default return shape** so that **I do not misjudge what the tool gives me and compensate by fetching more than I need**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered while implementing PR #3051 (documenting progressive-disclosure navigation), 2026-08-20\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 agents are choosing read strategies against an incomplete contract\\n- **Related**: PR #3051 (disclosure params, same drift class); #3050 (undefined ADRs, same \\\"design exists only in code\\\" pattern)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4444d6e75d205afd47e6dc301dd216df1a94ed44d4964b507e4ca41f14b0e0e2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuh8Ew\"}"}